stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(the pneumonia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If the inflammation is due to one of the various other germs that cause) Tj T*
(the remaining fifth of the pneumonia cases, still other treatment may) Tj T*
(be needed. It is clear, then, that your physician should be called) Tj T*
(promptly when pneumonia is suspected so that he may have the laboratory) Tj T*
(tests made that will tell him with what kind of germ infection he has) Tj T*
(to deal. Then he can decide what kind of treatment to employ.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                        Pneumonia Is Contagious) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pneumonia appears to be spread from person to person by contact, so it) Tj T*
(is regarded as a communicable disease. As it is contagious, the spread) Tj T*
(of infection can be stopped if precautions are taken to prevent the) Tj T*
(transfer of the infectious material from the sick to the well. The) Tj T*
(secretions from the nose and throat of persons sick with pneumonia,) Tj T*
(or convalescing from the disease, usually carry the germs that cause) Tj T*
(it. The transfer may take place through direct contact with these) Tj T*
(secretions, or inhaling droplets of moist sputum expelled by the sick) Tj T*
(person while coughing or sneezing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pneumonia is no respecter of persons. It may attack tiny babies, adults) Tj T*
(in the prime of life, or elderly people: so everyone must be on guard.) Tj T*
(This is especially true in late winter and early spring when the) Tj T*
(disease is most likely to occur.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pneumonia often begins during or just after an attack of the common) Tj T*
(cold, grippe, whooping cough, or measles, and after surgical operations,) Tj T*
(especially those upon the chest. In other conditions, such as unusual) Tj T*
(and prolonged fatigue or exposure to bad weather resulting in a thorough) Tj T*
(chilling, the chance of infection is increased.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                       Early Signs of Pneumonia) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In most cases of pneumonia the disease is readily recognized. There) Tj T*
(is often a preceding cold, but the onset of the pneumonia is usually) Tj T*
(abrupt, with sharp pain in the side, fever, a cough, a sense of) Tj T*
(chilliness or evident chills, and the expectoration of sputum streaked,) Tj T*
(or tinged, with blood.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Immediate medical and nursing care are vital in) Tj T*
(pneumonia._]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If you should ever have any of these early signs of pneumonia, get) Tj T*
(promptly into bed and stay there. Have your doctor called without a) Tj T*
(moment?s delay. You will improve your chance of a quick recovery if) Tj T*
(you give him the opportunity to determine the cause of your infection) Tj T*
(before it is many hours old. Remember: the longer the disease exists) Tj T*
(before treatment is begun, the more difficult it may prove to cure.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
