() Tj T*
(                           Finding the Cause) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The exact cause of the inflammation can be determined only by a) Tj T*
(laboratory examination of specimens of sputum or blood. Fortunately,) Tj T*
(in most sections of the country, diagnostic services are now readily) Tj T*
(available.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The kind of germ is determined earliest by examining specimens of) Tj T*
(sputum.[B] Though the patient may have some difficulty in raising) Tj T*
(sputum, enough for laboratory needs can almost always be obtained if) Tj T*
(its importance is explained to him. The expectorated material should) Tj T*
(come from the lungs, and should be as free as possible from mixture) Tj T*
(with saliva and nasal secretions. The sputum can be collected in) Tj T*
(any clean, wide-mouthed bottle, or a cardboard sputum box, and sent) Tj T*
(without delay to the nearest laboratory. Within a short time a report) Tj T*
(is returned to your doctor advising him of the findings of the) Tj T*
(examination. If pneumococci have been found, the special type will be) Tj T*
(named.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([B] Blood specimens are also of importance in diagnosis of the disease) Tj T*
(and determining the course of treatment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Laboratories are now equipped to make prompt and) Tj T*
(reliable examinations of sputum specimens._]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                       Hospital and Nursing Care) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The new drugs which have been found so successful in curing pneumonia) Tj T*
(occasionally make the patient nauseated and uncomfortable for a time.) Tj T*
(The curative serums which are used for certain types of pneumonia,) Tj T*
(also may sometimes produce unpleasant reactions temporarily. With both) Tj T*
(treatments it is essential that the patient be watched over by alert) Tj T*
(attendants at all times. Hence many doctors prefer that the pneumonia) Tj T*
(patient be taken to the hospital as soon as he becomes sick so that he) Tj T*
(can have the benefit of constant nursing care and so that everything) Tj T*
(possible may be done to avoid unpleasant reactions or allay the) Tj T*
(symptoms if they should occur.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If the patient must remain at home it is evident that he should have) Tj T*
(the best possible nursing care. When a full-time nurse is not to be) Tj T*
(in attendance, then the visiting nurse should be called in promptly.) Tj T*
(She not only will give the care to the patient that the doctor orders) Tj T*
(but will instruct the members of the family who must attend to the) Tj T*
(patient?s needs during her absence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to receiving the treatment already discussed, it is) Tj T*
(essential that the patient?s position in bed be changed at intervals to) Tj T*
(relieve congestion and increase comfort. From lying on his back he may) Tj T*
(be moved to one side or the other, but this, too, must be done for him.) Tj T*
(So, it is evident that constant care is vitally needed.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 10 0 R >>
