stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(The doctor?s orders must be followed to the last detail. Nothing) Tj T*
(is unimportant. The nurse will assist the attendants in following) Tj T*
(instructions. She will teach them what to observe in the patient?s) Tj T*
(condition, how to report the progress of the disease to the physician,[C]) Tj T*
(and will advise the members of the family how to prevent the spread of) Tj T*
(the patient?s infection to others in the household.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([C] The two booklets, ?Home Care of Communicable Diseases? and ?Caring) Tj T*
(for the Sick in the Home,? will prove useful as supplements to the) Tj T*
(nurse?s instruction. They are free for the asking.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                         Preventing Pneumonia) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In general, it may be said that a good physical condition of the body) Tj T*
(lessens the chance of an attack of pneumonia. A sensible balance of) Tj T*
(rest and exercise to prevent undue fatigue, eating nutritious meals,) Tj T*
(and avoiding over-exposure and chilling, all may help. It is the part) Tj T*
(of wisdom to stay indoors with a cold, and in bed while there is fever,) Tj T*
(for your own benefit as well as to prevent giving your infection to) Tj T*
(others.[D] While suffering from colds, grippe, tonsillitis, and the) Tj T*
(like, care should be taken to avoid exposure to draughts and rapid) Tj T*
(chilling of the body when overheated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([D] ?Living the Healthy Life? tells how to keep fit. ?What to Eat and) Tj T*
(Why? discusses the question of diet. ?That Mean Cold? tells more in) Tj T*
(detail about the care of colds. Copies of all these booklets will be) Tj T*
(sent to anyone on request.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Overcrowding greatly increases the chance of spreading pneumonia) Tj T*
(from person to person. When colds and other respiratory diseases are) Tj T*
(prevalent, public gatherings should be avoided as much as possible.) Tj T*
(Rules of health departments forbidding spitting should be strictly) Tj T*
(obeyed by all. Special precautions should be taken against unnecessary) Tj T*
(contact with pneumonia patients and those recently recovered from) Tj T*
(the disease, who still may be carriers of the germ. This precaution) Tj T*
(is especially important for persons who are run down, or have some) Tj T*
(existing respiratory disease.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the care of patients with pneumonia, the following precautions for) Tj T*
(the protection of others must be observed:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If the patient is treated at home, only those responsible for his care) Tj T*
(should be permitted in the sick-room.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The patient?s nasal discharges and sputum should be collected in pieces) Tj T*
(of cloth or soft paper and burned promptly. Droplet infection may be) Tj T*
(avoided by placing a piece of cloth or soft paper over the patient?s) Tj T*
(mouth when he coughs or sneezes, and this cloth or paper should be) Tj T*
(burned. Unnecessary contamination of bedding or clothing should be) Tj T*
(prevented.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
