stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(The patient?s eating utensils, bedding, and linen should be scalded and) Tj T*
(washed in soap and hot water.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dry sweeping or dusting of the sick-room should not be permitted;) Tj T*
(cleaning can be done safely only with a damp cloth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After each time that care is given to the patient, the attendant should) Tj T*
(scrub her hands thoroughly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Articles which cannot be washed should be thoroughly aired and exposed) Tj T*
(to sunlight out-of-doors for a day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Dressed for the weather, outdoor exercise keeps the) Tj T*
(body fit._]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                  Points to Remember about Pneumonia) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pneumonia may attack without warning, but often is preceded by a cold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If chills, fever, pain in the chest, and sputum tinged with blood) Tj T*
(occur, it is a signal to get to bed promptly and have the doctor called) Tj T*
(immediately.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(New drugs have proved to be of great benefit in treatment, but for) Tj T*
(certain types of pneumonia both drugs and serum may be needed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Good nursing care is vital. If the patient is not to be treated in) Tj T*
(a hospital, provision should be made for a full-time nurse, or for) Tj T*
(regular care by the visiting nurse.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
